					"uidString" : "HxpDgJycRwqh3xkM30AxRA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The cellsFormat property determines how numeric, date, and time values are presented in libraries like Smart HTML Elements and jQWidgets.The string format consists of a letter defining the style type, optionally followed by a number specifying the decimal places. \n\nFor example, 'c2' specifies a currency format (c) with exactly 2 decimal places (2).\n\nNumber Formatting OptionsFor numeric values, you can swap 'c2' with any of the following letters:\n\nc\t(Currency): Formats the value with a currency symbol and thousand separators based on the\n\t\t system locale (e.g., 'c0' → $1,235, 'c3' → $1,234.568)\n\nFormats standard integer numbers.\nf\t(Floating-point): Displays fixed-point notation (e.g., 'f4' → 1234.5678)\nn\t(Integer / Number): Displays numbers with a thousand separator (e.g., 'n2' → 1,234.57)\np\t(Percentage): Multiplies the value by 100 and appends a percent symbol (e.g., 'p1' → 75.5%).\n\nDate and Time Formatting Options\nIf your column data consists of Date objects or ISO timestamp strings, you can use these standard case-sensitive letters:\nd \t(Short Date): Standard regional format (e.g., M/d/yyyy → 8/11/2026).\nD \t(Long Date): Full text day and month (e.g., dddd, MMMM dd, yyyy → Tuesday, August 11, 2026).\nt\t  (Short Time): Hours and minutes (e.g., h:mm tt → 4:06 PM).\nT \t(Long Time): Includes seconds (e.g., h:mm:ss tt → 4:06:15 PM).\nf \t(Long Date, Short Time): Combines day, month, and time without seconds.\nF \t(Long Date, Long Time): Full day, month, and precise timestamp.\nM\t(Month/Day): Displays only month and day (e.g., August 11).\nY \t(Month/Year): Displays only month and year (e.g., 2026 August).\nS \t(Sortable ISO): A culture-invariant string (yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss).\n\nWould you like to see how to change the regional currency symbol (e.g., switching from USD to EUR) or do you need help setting up a custom custom-date pattern format?"
			},
